{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevH9Q5WE6Tgr9cC5U1ze","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me proceed to the design phase.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add a new ErrorCode enum value `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to represent the error when trying to confirm a `CANCELLED` shipment. This error will be thrown with a 409 Conflict status via the existing `ConflictException` mechanism.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID (throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found)\n   - If status is `CREATED`, changes it to `CONFIRMED` and saves\n   - If status is `CONFIRMED`, does nothing (idempotent)\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throws `ConflictException` with the new error code\n   - Returns the shipment as a 200 OK response\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and changes nothing\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with correct error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with correct error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\nI considered adding a new exception class like `CannotConfirmException`, but rejected it because:\n- `ConflictException` is already the pattern used for state conflicts (see `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`)\n- The error handling is centralized; adding a new exception type would be architectural clutter\n- The existing exception + error code pattern scales well\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Happy path (CREATED→CONFIRMED):** POST `/shipments/{id}/confirm` → repository.findById() → status == CREATED → update to CONFIRMED → save → 200 OK with Shipment\n- **Idempotent case (already CONFIRMED):** POST `/shipments/{id}/confirm` → repository.findById() → status == CONFIRMED → no change → save unchanged → 200 OK with Shipment\n- **Invalid state (CANCELLED):** POST `/shipments/{id}/confirm` → repository.findById() → status == CANCELLED → throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM) → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it → 409 Conflict with ApiError envelope\n- **Not found:** POST `/shipments/{id}/confirm` → repository.findById() returns null → throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it → 404 Not Found with ApiError envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **confirm_created_shipment**: Create shipment, confirm it, assert status changed to CONFIRMED and returned\n2. **confirm_already_confirmed_shipment**: Create and confirm shipment, confirm again, assert 200 OK and status still CONFIRMED\n3. **confirm_cancelled_shipment**: Create and manually set to CANCELLED in repository, confirm, assert 409 Conflict with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n4. **confirm_non_existent_shipment**: Confirm non-existent ID, assert 404 Not Found with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":414,"cache_read_input_tokens":18952,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":414},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a7061e2-caf1-4491-829b-15d008fde927","uuid":"e41e47d8-9796-4d96-b404-dc8b2ad3bbb2","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:04:22.627Z","request_id":"req_011CevH9PP5yLLoGr8eeZqRw"}
